// ─── resource-catalogue.js — the patient & family resources (2026-10-22 `resqr`) ───
//
// ONE list, three readers:
//   · the app (ui/index.html loads it) — the Extra tab's 📚 Resources picker (extra-notes.js) and its ▦ QR
//     (ui/src/resource-qr.js), Settings › Patient Handouts (db-editor-module.js);
//   · the family's page (viewer/resource-catalogue.js is a byte-for-byte COPY of this file — run
//     `node scripts/build-resource-catalogue.mjs` after any change: it copies it and regenerates the watch's list);
//   · the Apple Watch (AnotaWatch/…/ResourceCatalog.swift, GENERATED by the same script).
//
// Per user: "the QR code needs to present the different resources each a click away, an easily navigable page
// for families"; "the resources (pdfs or files) need to be disseminated instantly … it shouldn't rely on other
// webpages unless we are sending over the link to a webpage itself"; the page is titled "Patient and Family
// Resource Page".
//
//   THE LINK IS THE LIST. A QR carries `<viewer>#R1.<code>.<code>…` (e.g. `https://anota-app.github.io/#R1.U1.U3`):
//   the codes of the chosen entries and nothing else — no patient, no expiry, no server row. The page reads the
//   codes from its #fragment (a browser never sends a fragment) and draws the entries from ITS copy of this file.
//   A doctor's own resource (one he added in Settings, not in this list) rides inline as `X<base64url JSON
//   [title, url]>`. Four codes make a ~45-character link: a version-4 QR (33 modules), easy to scan off a watch.
//   THE LANGUAGE the page opens in rides as one lower-case word after `R1` — `#R1.fr.U1.U3` (`en` · `fr`; no word =
//   the phone's language). It is the doctor's choice, Settings › Patient Handouts › "The family's page opens in"
//   (chrome.storage `patientResourcesLang`, synced: `fr` · `en` · `phone`; unset = LANG_DEFAULT). The family can
//   still switch at the top of the page. A code is a capital and digits, so the word can never be read as one.
//
//   `file: true` — the PDF is hosted beside the page (viewer/docs/<code>.<lang>.pdf, copied from the source on
//   2026-10-22): a tap opens it at once from the same site. `kind: 'page'` — the resource IS a web page; the
//   card opens it. Every entry has a preview, viewer/previews/<code>.<lang>.webp (720×450, the top of page 1 /
//   of the page). `only: 'fr'` — the source has no English version; both languages show the French file.
//   `url` / `url_fr` are always the SOURCE's address (the note prints it; the hosted copy is the page's).
//
// Codes are stable forever (an old QR must keep opening the same thing): never reuse or renumber one; a retired
// entry keeps its code out of use (C9, CHEO's strep-throat index page, was replaced by P2 before it shipped).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

